# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Our World — environment
#
# IMPORTANT, READ FIRST
#
# The app as it stands needs NO environment variables and NO secrets. It is a
# static page. Storage, auth and photo hosting are all provided by the Claude
# Artifacts runtime at page-open time (window.claude), so there is no API key
# to configure and nothing to rotate. `npm run dev` works on a clean clone with
# no .env file at all.
#
# This file exists for two reasons:
#   1. PORT, the only variable the dev server reads today.
#   2. The variables you WILL need if you migrate off the Claude runtime onto
#      your own backend. They are commented out because nothing reads them yet.
#      Wiring them up means writing an adapter — see README "Migrating off the
#      Claude runtime".
#
# Copy to .env and edit. .env is gitignored. Never commit real keys.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Local dev server port (dev/serve.js). Default 4173.
PORT=4173


# ── ONLY IF YOU MIGRATE TO YOUR OWN BACKEND ─────────────────────────────────
# Nothing below is read by the current code.

# --- Option A: Firebase / Firestore -----------------------------------------
# Closest match to the current data model: document collections, live snapshots,
# last-writer-wins. Firebase Storage replaces photo assets.
# FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-app.firebaseapp.com
# FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-app.appspot.com
# FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
# FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# --- Option B: Supabase ------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres + Realtime + Storage. Use the ANON key in the browser and enforce
# row-level security; never ship the service-role key to the client.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxx.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=our-world-photos

# --- Auth --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Today "who am I" is a per-device choice in localStorage (bruce | elena) with
# no authentication at all. Real accounts need a provider.
# AUTH_PROVIDER=
# AUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Optional: real map tiles ------------------------------------------------
# The current build embeds its own geography and needs no tile server. If you
# move to a host without the Artifacts CSP you could add real tiles instead.
# MAP_TILE_URL=https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
# MAPTILER_KEY=
# MAPBOX_TOKEN=

# --- Optional: geocoding -----------------------------------------------------
# Region names currently come from an embedded town list (nearest-town lookup),
# not a geocoder. A real reverse geocoder would name places more precisely.
# GEOCODER_PROVIDER=
# GEOCODER_KEY=
